  "notes": [
    "Opus codec (float build) for the Ogg Opus source decoder of the audio importer (Docs/Design/AudioSystem.ko.md section 3.29); the Opus encoder for cooking and the client runtime decoder (AudioOpus) will link the same library later.",
    "No SIMD sources and no runtime CPU detection (OPUS_X86_MAY_HAVE_* and OPUS_HAVE_RTCD are not defined), so decoded samples are fixed per architecture and compiler flags (section 3.10.1).",
    "Defines follow the upstream CMake defaults: VAR_ARRAYS (C99 variable-length arrays instead of alloca), HAVE_LRINTF and HAVE_LRINT, and ENABLE_HARDENING (cheap invariant checks that stay on in release builds). PACKAGE_VERSION is not defined, so opus_get_version_string reports 'libopus unknown'.",
    "Opus.Build.cs adds the library-internal include directories (celt, silk, silk/float, src) to the library build only, so that headers with common names (debug.h, errors.h, main.h) do not reach consuming modules through includeDirectories."
  ]
}
